---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Card } from "../../components/ui/card";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer";
import {
  TrendingUp,
  Shield,
  Clock,
  FileText,
  Search,
} from "lucide-react";
---

<Layout
  title="Private Client Meeting Notes for Financial Advisors on Mac | Summit"
  description="Client meeting notes for financial advisors on your Mac, with no bot joining the call. Local transcription and summaries; optional cloud AI is your choice."
  breadcrumb={[{ name: "For Finance Professionals" }]}
>
  <div
    class="min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-background via-background to-muted/20"
  >
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-16">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="text-center mb-16">
          <div
            class="w-16 h-16 bg-green-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-6"
          >
            <TrendingUp className="w-8 h-8 text-green-600" />
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">
            Client meeting notes for financial advisors, kept on your Mac
          </h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground">
            Reviews, planning sessions and discovery calls each need a clear
            record you can come back to. Summit turns recorded conversations
            into transcripts and summaries on your Mac, with folders to organize
            clients and search to revisit what was discussed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Where notes are processed -->
        <Card
          className="p-8 mb-12 bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-blue-50 border-green-200"
        >
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">
            You choose where client conversations are processed
          </h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            Transcription runs on your Mac, and there is no Summit account
            holding your meeting library. Select Local Models and summaries and
            chat run on your Mac too. If you choose a cloud AI provider, the
            relevant transcript text is sent to that provider, so review that
            setting before recording client conversations. Markdown auto-export
            and iCloud sync are off until you turn them on.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            Recording consent, your firm's policies and your regulatory
            obligations still apply. The
            <a href="/security/architecture" class="text-blue-600 underline"
              >architecture page</a
            > lists exactly what is stored and what can leave your Mac.
          </p>
        </Card>

        <!-- Client workflow -->
        <Card
          className="p-8 mb-12 bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-blue-50 border-green-200"
        >
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">
            Keep each client's context separate in your workflow
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="flex gap-4">
              <div
                class="w-8 h-8 bg-green-600 text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 font-bold"
              >
                1
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">
                  Create a folder for each client or household
                </h3>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                  Give every relationship its own folder, and optionally a
                  folder
                  <a
                    href="/docs/guides/summary-templates"
                    class="text-blue-600 underline">summary template</a
                  > so reviews and planning sessions are written up the same
                  way.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-4">
              <div
                class="w-8 h-8 bg-green-600 text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 font-bold"
              >
                2
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">
                  Use clear meeting titles
                </h3>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                  Name meetings with the client and meeting type, so the right
                  conversation is easy to spot in search results.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-4">
              <div
                class="w-8 h-8 bg-green-600 text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 font-bold"
              >
                3
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">
                  Check the scope before you ask
                </h3>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                  Filter search by folder, or select that client's meetings and
                  chat about just those. The chat shows which meetings are
                  included before you ask a question.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-4">
              <div
                class="w-8 h-8 bg-green-600 text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 font-bold"
              >
                4
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">
                  Open the original passage
                </h3>
                <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                  Chat answers cite timestamped transcript passages. Check the
                  source before copying a goal, figure or decision into your
                  CRM or a client follow-up.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-6">
            Folders help organize notes; they are not a separate account,
            encrypted vault or access-control boundary.
          </p>
        </Card>

        <!-- Records and compliance -->
        <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">
            Notes, not a compliance archive
          </h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            Summit is a note-taking tool. It is not a books-and-records system,
            communications archive or supervision tool, and using it does not by
            itself meet SEC, FINRA, MiFID or other recordkeeping requirements.
            Check your firm's recordkeeping and supervision rules before
            recording client meetings, and decide where any notes you keep as
            official records should live.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            Summaries are a starting point, not a guarantee that every detail
            was captured. Use the original transcript to check amounts, dates
            and commitments.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Key Benefits -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8 text-center">
            Why Finance Professionals Choose Summit
          </h2>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <Card className="p-6">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div
                  class="w-10 h-10 bg-green-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center"
                >
                  <Clock className="w-5 h-5 text-green-600" />
                </div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">
                  Start From a Draft
                </h3>
              </div>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Summit drafts a summary with key points and action items after
                each recording, so your meeting notes start from a draft instead
                of a blank page.
              </p>
            </Card>

            <Card className="p-6">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div
                  class="w-10 h-10 bg-blue-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center"
                >
                  <Shield className="w-5 h-5 text-blue-600" />
                </div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">
                  No Meeting Bot
                </h3>
              </div>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Summit records from your Mac instead of joining the call as a
                participant, for video calls and in-person meetings alike.
              </p>
            </Card>

            <Card className="p-6">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div
                  class="w-10 h-10 bg-purple-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center"
                >
                  <FileText className="w-5 h-5 text-purple-600" />
                </div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">
                  Consistent Meeting Write-Ups
                </h3>
              </div>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Summary templates shape notes for annual reviews, discovery
                meetings and planning sessions.
              </p>
            </Card>

            <Card className="p-6">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div
                  class="w-10 h-10 bg-orange-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center"
                >
                  <Search className="w-5 h-5 text-orange-600" />
                </div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">
                  Recall With Sources
                </h3>
              </div>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Search past meetings for a client's goals, concerns or earlier
                decisions, and follow chat citations back to the passage in the
                transcript.
              </p>
            </Card>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Use Cases -->
        <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">Perfect For</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <Card className="p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">
                Financial Advisors & Wealth Managers
              </h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Take notes from discovery meetings, quarterly reviews and
                planning sessions, then find what a client said about goals or
                concerns before the next review.
              </p>
            </Card>

            <Card className="p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">
                Investment Analysts
              </h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Keep notes from management calls, investor briefings and
                research discussions, and search them when you revisit a
                thesis.
              </p>
            </Card>

            <Card className="p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">
                Financial Planners
              </h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Record intake sessions and draft summaries of goals and
                circumstances, then check the transcript before building the
                plan.
              </p>
            </Card>

            <Card className="p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-foreground mb-3">
                Private Bankers
              </h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground">
                Keep a folder for each relationship so earlier discussions about
                lending, estate planning or investments are easy to find.
              </p>
            </Card>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- CTA -->
        <Card
          className="p-8 bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-blue-50 border-green-200 text-center"
        >
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">
            Try Summit on your next client meeting
          </h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-6">
            Summit runs on macOS. Choose Local Models in AI settings to keep
            summaries and chat on your Mac.
          </p>
          <a
            href="/download?from=use-case-cta"
            data-source="use-case-cta"
            class="download-button inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 bg-green-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-green-700 transition-colors"
          >
            See Mac download options
          </a>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Footer client:load />
</Layout>

<style>
  :global(.dark) .prose {
    --tw-prose-body: var(--foreground);
    --tw-prose-headings: var(--foreground);
  }
</style>
